[95.258382, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 handoff\n\n## Fixed\n\n- Calendar arithmetic incorrectly clamped every date to the 28th and advanced\n  from previously clamped renewals. It now clamps to the target month's last\n  day and calculates both cycle boundaries from the original anchor, restoring\n  month-end and leap-day renewals without drift.\n- Proration used fixed 30/365-day denominators and credited the old plan at its\n  change-date price. It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at the\n  cycle start; the new plan uses its change-date price.\n- Monthly/annual switches now charge a full new interval and re-anchor on the\n  change date, with the correct next renewal and invoice line period.\n- Half-even rounding now uses exact integer division, independent of Decimal\n  precision. Public function signatures are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll ten finance examples pass, including through `python -m billing preview`.\nNine added regression tests cover boundaries, Gregorian leap rules, exact\nroundin"]
[95.258622, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # BILL-212 handoff"]
[95.258641, "i", "g, pricing dates, invoice lines, and CLI output.\n\n`python -m unittest discover -s tests` currently runs 26 tests: 25 pass and one\nerrors. All original calendar and finance-example failures are resolved.\n\n## Release blocker: missing contracted partner rate\n\nThe remaining error also occurred before these changes:\n`PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines` raises `KeyError: 'P-31'`.\n`data/subscriptions.json` assigns sub_1151 (cus_islay_freight) to P-31, but\n`data/partners.json` defines only P-12, P-17, and P-24. No P-31 commission rate\nor contract is provided in the repository.\n\nFinance must supply P-31's contracted rate/partner record, or confirm a corrected\npartner ID for sub_1151. Then rerun the full suite before releasing. No rate has\nbeen guessed, no subscription removed, and no tests skipped or quarantined.\nThe release gate is still red; this change is not yet cleared to ship.\nEOF\nPYTHONPATH=tests python -m unittest test_calendar test_proration.WorkedExamplesTest test_proration.PortionTest test_pro"]
[95.258649, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[95.258654, "i", "ration.InvoiceTest test_bill212_regressions\n"]
