[95.262117, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   day and calculates both cycle boundaries from the original anchor, restoring\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   month-end and leap-day renewals without drift.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Proration used fixed 30/365-day denominators and credited the old plan at its\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   change-date price. It now uses actual cycle days and the price billed at the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   cycle start; the new plan uses its change-date price.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Monthly/annual switches now charge a full new interval and re-anchor on the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   change date, with the correct next renewal and invoice line period.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Half-even rounding now uses exact integer division, independent of Decimal\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   precision. Public function signatures are unchanged.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Verification\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> All ten finance examples pass, including through `python -m billing preview`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Nine added regression test"]
[95.262138, "o", "s cover boundaries, Gregorian leap rules, exact\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> rounding, pricing dates, invoice lines, and CLI output.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[95.262421, "o", "`python -m unittest discover -s tests` currently runs 26 tests: 25 pass and one"]
[95.263871, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> errors. All original calendar and finance-example failures are resolved.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Release blocker: missing contracted partner rate\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The remaining error also occurred before these changes:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines` raises `KeyError: 'P-31'`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `data/subscriptions.json` assigns sub_1151 (cus_islay_freight) to P-31, but\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `data/partners.json` defines only P-12, P-17, and P-24. No P-31 commission rate\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> or contract is provided in the repository.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Finance must supply P-31's contracted rate/partner record, or confirm a corrected\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> partner ID for sub_1151. Then rerun the full suite before releasing. No rate has\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> been guessed, no subscription removed, and no tests skipped or quarantined.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The release gate is still red; this change "]
[95.26421, "o", "is not yet cleared to ship.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
